# .dockerignore
#
# Controls what gets sent to the Docker daemon as build context when you
# run `docker build .` from the repo root.
#
# --- Why this file matters more here than in a typical project ---
# Without it, EVERY build uploads the entire repo root as context --
# including data/, which for this app holds reference genomes, STAR
# indices, downloaded FASTQ files, and BAMs. On a real deployment that is
# routinely tens to hundreds of GB. The symptom is a build that appears
# to hang for many minutes at "transferring context" before a single
# instruction runs, on every rebuild, even for a one-line code change.
#
# Excluding data/ is also a correctness matter, not just speed: the
# container gets its data directory from the volume mount at runtime (see
# docker-compose.yml). Baking a stale copy into the image would shadow
# nothing at runtime but would bloat the image by the full size of
# whatever happened to be on disk at build time.

# --- Runtime data (mounted at runtime, never baked into the image) ---
data/
**/data/projects/
**/data/singlecell_projects/
**/data/shared_references/
**/data/shared_whitelists/
**/data/marker_libraries/
**/data/monitor/

# --- Credentials: must never enter an image layer ---
# Image layers are readable by anyone who can pull the image, and
# deleting a file in a later layer does NOT remove it from the earlier
# layer that added it.
**/data/auth/
.env
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# --- Version control ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Python bytecode / caches ---
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Virtual environments (the image builds its own from environment.yml) ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
miniforge3/
miniconda3/

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# --- Local scratch that shouldn't ship (mirrors .gitignore) ---
docs/
recover_kang_bam.py

# --- Logs and transient state ---
*.log
**/monitor.log
**/monitor.pid
**/setup_install_log.txt
**/*.corrupt-*

# --- Large bioinformatics artifacts that may be sitting in the tree ---
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq
*.fq.gz
*.bam
*.sam
*.h5ad
*.rds

# --- R project cruft ---
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData

# --- Docker's own files (not needed inside the image) ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
